# declared skips for the mos6502 column. one entry per line:
#   <case-glob>  <layers>[:<profiles>]  <reason>
# layers is any of a, b, c, or * for all three. naming pipelines after a colon
# declares away those cells and no others. a skip counts as a skip in the matrix,
# never as a pass, and the run fails on an empty cell that has no entry here.
#
# layer c needs no entry: engines.conf declares engine none for this target, which
# the matrix reports as its own label.

* ab no case builds for mos6502, all 91 of them. the backend refuses with "mir.lower_ir: target has no float/vector register bank" because corpus.lib.fold carries mix_f32 and mix_f64, and behind that sits the same 64-bit gap riscv32 hits, since the fold accumulator is a u64 the contract requires of every case. reopening this column means splitting the fold prelude so an integer-only case pulls no float helper, AND landing wide-value lowering for an 8-bit machine. da65 gets a tools.lock pin then, not before: pinning a version nothing here has run against would be a claim rather than a record.
